WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
Battery performance changes with temperature.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:10.999
In cold conditions, chemical reactions slow and voltage may sag under load, reducing usable energy and power.

00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:17.379
A battery that appears charged can reach a critical state sooner than expected.

00:00:17.379 --> 00:00:21.559
Follow approved guidance for battery temperature and preconditioning.

00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:31.018
Keep batteries in a suitable environment before use, confirm they have reached an acceptable operating condition, and avoid improvised heating.

00:00:31.018 --> 00:00:35.638
Plan shorter flights and larger reserves in the cold.

00:00:35.638 --> 00:00:38.058
Heat creates different risks.

00:00:38.058 --> 00:00:47.517
High ambient temperature, direct sun, heavy processing, hovering, and repeated flights can stress batteries, motors, electronics, mobile devices, and payloads.

00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:53.017
Overheated components may throttle, shut down, age faster, or behave unpredictably.

00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:56.317
Monitor more than a percentage display.

00:00:56.317 --> 00:01:07.536
Observe voltage or cell status when available, temperature warnings, power demand, battery age, prior damage, swelling, and the difference between planned and actual consumption.

00:01:07.536 --> 00:01:11.716
Treat unexpected behavior as a reason to recover.

00:01:11.716 --> 00:01:14.576
Storage and transport affect safety.

00:01:14.576 --> 00:01:21.395
Protect batteries from physical damage, moisture, extreme temperature, conductive objects, and unattended hot vehicles.

00:01:21.395 --> 00:01:28.655
Use approved charging, storage, and retirement practices, and isolate questionable batteries according to organizational procedures.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:31.955
Temperature also affects people and data.

00:01:31.955 --> 00:01:38.334
Cold hands, heat stress, screen dimming, condensation, and sensor drift can degrade decisions.

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:45.154
Environmental planning includes crew endurance and payload quality as well as aircraft flight time.
